{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018TVEMdjWAdNeTRhPBrTmCB","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-0rA7w7/README.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9451c4e7-7bb1-4a4b-8b33-6d068fbea43d","uuid":"7e768ee2-b700-424a-8d72-2c6b7b8d29f8","timestamp":"2026-11-10T03:11:22.157Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-0rA7w7/README.md","oldString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","newString":"Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt is two blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. Block 1 is the static\ncoaching instructions (byte-identical for everyone); block 2 is the per-athlete\ntail (date, profile, facts). A `save_fact` write only re-caches block 2. Tests:\n`python3 -m unittest tests/test_cache_split.py`.","originalFile":"# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":5,"newStart":12,"newLines":7,"lines":[" messages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs"," `COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`)."," Requires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system","-prompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up","-messages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","+prompt is two blocks, each with a `cache_control` marker. Block 1 is the static","+coaching instructions (byte-identical for everyone); block 2 is the per-athlete","+tail (date, profile, facts). A `save_fact` write only re-caches block 2. Tests:","+`python3 -m unittest tests/test_cache_split.py`."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018TVEMdjWAdNeTRhPBrTmCB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
