{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtWrAfCkHnyJUBuFhYGb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I split the system prompt into two cached blocks, so a `save_fact` write should only re-cache the per-athlete tail. Whether that saves anything depends on a size threshold I could not confirm live, and it may not hold for this prompt.\n\n**What changed**\n- `bot.py`, `build_system()`: block 1 is the static `INSTRUCTIONS`, byte-identical for every athlete and day. Block 2 is the athlete context (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language). Both carry `cache_control`.\n- `tests/test_cache_split.py` (new): 4 offline tests, all passing. They check the layout, that block 1 is identical across athletes and days, that a fact write changes only block 2, and that block 1 has no interpolated values.\n- `README.md`: the caching paragraph describes the new layout.\n- `ANSWER.md`: the write-up, including which parts of the colleague's note applied.\n\nNothing is committed.\n\n**Risk: the 1024-token minimum.** Sonnet only caches a prefix of at least 1024 tokens. My estimate for block 1 plus tool definitions is roughly 950–1000 tokens, calibrated against the logged `cache_creation_input_tokens: 1046`. If that holds, block 1 won't cache on its own. The fix then gains nothing for memory writes, though it does no harm. Growing `INSTRUCTIONS` by a few hundred characters of real guidance would fix it, but that is a content decision, so I didn't pad it.\n\n**Not verified live.** I had no API key and couldn't make a call. `ANSWER.md` lists the check to run on the next live messages: after a `save_fact`, `cache_read` should cover block 1 and `cache_creation` should be about the size of block 2.\n\n**Not changed.** Tool-group switching (for example the `plan` group) changes the tools array, which sits before the system prompt, so it still re-caches everything. That is a known trade-off in `NOTES.md`, and I left it alone."}],"co